@IT_Howard (14:02): Has anyone else noticed our office reporting software crashing with "Out of Memory" errors after upgrading to v3.1? Our daily reports haven't changed, yet memory usage jumped 25%.
@Support_Nina (14:09): Check your memory-limit setting! In v3.1, the updated program enforces system memory limits more strictly. If the maximum memory percentage isn't set in the preferences menu, the software tries to use too much host memory.
@IT_Howard (14:15): Good catch—let me inspect the setup file. Right now we only specify a 2 GB general limit, nothing for the maximum percentage.
@Systems_Leo (14:22): Also verify the background activity tracker. We saw a similar spike last month when the tracker saved temporary files locally during a main database slowdown.
@IT_Howard (14:35): Update: Nina was right! Setting the maximum memory percentage to 75% stabilized all six computers immediately. Thanks, everyone!
